      "side": 1,
      "message": "I believe the way this implemented it controls the max buffered + running? If we consider MAX_TASKS_IN_FLIGHT the sum of two other values MAX_BUFFERED and MAX_THREADS, and we want to match the current plugin behavior as close as possible without blocking the requests creating events unless the system cannot keep up, we would set MAX_BUFFERED to 0, and MAX_THREADS to the current value of threads which can create events. So, I suggest we start by setting this to MAX_THREADS.\n\nAs a follow on change idea (by no means do we need to do this), we may want to support a config which supports somehow have a mode which can be used to figure out all the sources of events and automatically set MAX_THREADS to the number of threads which can create events.\n\nA separate follow on idea is to make MAX_BUFFERED configurable so it need not be 0, but 0 is probably a good value in most situations.\n\nOne concern I have with the current semaphore approach is that it is not amenable to virtual threads, but it is simple enough to change easily, and fairly clean I think.",
